near/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"question" "q-140539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$  \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$  \n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{0\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B={{u}_{1},{u}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an  orthonormal basis of $V.$   \n\nFinally, $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ $c=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}|+|\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}|+|-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}|=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"question" "q-140539" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9921c61e8a2def5f859b3c22e7e48c790ef5fc52270d26a70301c7efbd7d2a1d"} {"question" "q-140539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"question" "q-140539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"question" "q-140539" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"question" "q-40743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,B={{u}_{1},{u}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]}\n$$\n\nConsider the subspace $\\text{Col}(A)$ and an **orthonormal** basis $B$ of $\\text{Col}(A),$ where $A$ and $B$ are given above. Given that $B$ is derived from $\\text{Col}(A)$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $|a|+|b|+|c|?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"question" "q-40743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that $\\text{Col}(A)$ is the span of the columns of $A.$  \n\nFirst, let's denote\n\n$\\,$ ${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nWe proceed to find an orthogonal basis using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows.\n\n**Step 1**: We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n**Step 2**: Next, we find ${v}_{2}$, by using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the formula for ${v}_{2}$ in our case gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize each vector to get an orthonormal basis:\n\n- ${u}_{1}=\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- ${u}_{2}=\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, $B={{v}_{1},{v}_{2}}={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}]}$ is an orthonormal basis for $\\text{Col}(A).$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3},$ $c=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ and  \n\n$$\n|a|+|b|+|c|=|-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}|+|\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}|+|\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}|=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"question" "q-40743" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9921c61e8a2def5f859b3c22e7e48c790ef5fc52270d26a70301c7efbd7d2a1d"} {"question" "q-40743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"question" "q-40743" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070290/state.json" "file_sha256" "17f114862f8bc295086bfd6ca75eb6d0dd2e240f3680f1e892861a2def005131"} {"